{{!< default}}
{{!-- WHS Brief: jurisdiction register. Not a new content type — reorganises
the same #brief post content already rendered on /brief/, grouped by
jurisdiction (.wbd-juris id) instead of by week.

How this works, and why:
  - Ghost posts are opaque HTML blobs, not structured objects, so there's no
    native way to query "every NSW item across all weeks." Rather than add a
    second weekly-maintained data source (more moving parts, and the theme's
    deploy pipeline needs manual approval per push — see
    .github/workflows/deploy-to-ghost-pro.yml — so anything requiring a
    weekly deploy doesn't fit this site's cadence), this page derives the
    register live, client-side, from content Ghost is already serving.
  - {{content}} inside the {{#get}}/{{#foreach}} loop below renders each
    post's full content through Ghost's normal member-gating (same as any
    other page) — a non-paying visitor gets the usual locked/teaser markup,
    a paying member gets the full .whs-brief-doc HTML. The register never
    bypasses this: it only ever reorganises whatever Ghost already decided
    to send to this specific visitor.
  - The source posts are rendered into a hidden container; script.js (loaded
    site-wide, see default.hbs) walks that container, finds every
    .whs-brief-doc .wbd-juris section per post, and regroups their .wbd-item
    children by jurisdiction into the visible tabbed view below. See
    assets/js/register.js for that logic.
  - Known tradeoff: every post's .wbd-juris sections reuse the same ids
    (id="national", id="nsw", ...), so this hidden container has duplicate
    DOM ids across posts — invalid HTML strictly speaking, but harmless here
    since register.js reads `.id` as a string per post block via
    querySelectorAll scoped to that block, never via a page-wide
    getElementById lookup.
  - limit="26" caps this to roughly the last six months of weekly briefs to
    keep the page from slowing down as the archive grows. Older material is
    still reachable via the flat chronological list at /brief/.
--}}

<main id="site-main" class="site-main outer">
<div class="inner posts">

    <div class="whs-brief-doc">
        <div class="wbd-masthead">
            <p class="wbd-eyebrow">Work Health &amp; Safety — Legislative Register</p>
            <h1>Browse every change by jurisdiction</h1>
            <p class="wbd-dek">The same weekly brief content, indexed by state and territory instead of by week, so you can pull up everything relevant to one jurisdiction without paging back through past issues.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <nav class="wbd-register-tabs" id="wbd-register-tabs" aria-label="Filter by jurisdiction">
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab is-active" data-jur="all">All</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="national">National</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="nsw">NSW</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="vic">VIC</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="qld">QLD</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="wa">WA</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="sa">SA</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="tas">TAS</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="act">ACT</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="nt">NT</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="nz">NZ</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="standards">Standards</button>
        <button type="button" class="wbd-register-tab" data-jur="courts">Courts</button>
    </nav>

    <div id="wbd-register-output" class="wbd-register-output">
        <p class="wbd-register-loading">Loading register…</p>
    </div>

    <p class="wbd-register-footnote">Showing roughly the last six months of weekly briefs. For anything older, browse the <a href="{{@site.url}}/brief/">full archive</a>.</p>

    {{!-- Hidden source data: full content of recent #brief posts, for
    register.js to parse. Never shown directly. --}}
    <div id="wbd-register-source" hidden>
        {{#get "posts" filter="tag:brief" limit="26" order="published_at desc" include="tags,authors" as |posts|}}
            {{#foreach posts}}
                <div class="wbd-register-post"
                     data-title="{{title}}"
                     data-url="{{url}}"
                     data-date="{{date format="DD MMM YYYY"}}">
                    {{content}}
                </div>
            {{/foreach}}
        {{/get}}
    </div>

</div>
</main>
